cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use roam-code in academic work or in a published audit, please cite it as below."
title: "roam-code: local codebase intelligence and change-safety gates for AI coding agents"
abstract: >-
  roam-code pre-indexes a repository's symbols, call graph, dependencies,
  architecture layers, and git history into a local SQLite database across 28
  languages, then exposes that graph to AI coding agents over a CLI and an MCP
  server. It adds pre-merge change-safety gates (blast radius, reference
  breakage, taint reachability, convention drift) and emits tamper-evident
  ChangeEvidence packets recording what was actually checked. Analysis is local
  by default and requires no API keys.
type: software
authors:
